# 🛠️ Technology Stack & Workflow Rules

You are an expert in modern Rust, WebAssembly, and cross-platform development. You must strictly adhere to the following technology stack and tooling versions when generating code, suggesting architectures, or debugging.

## 📦 Core Technology Stack

### Backend & Fullstack
- **Language**: Rust 1.88.0+
- **Web Frameworks**: Leptos 0.8.x (Frontend/Fullstack), Axum 0.8.x (Backend API)
- **Async Runtime**: Tokio
- **Databases & Storage**: SQLite (Relational), Fjall 3.x (Embedded KV), Tonbo (LSM-Tree KV)

### WebAssembly & Edge Computing
- **Runtimes & Deployment**: Wasmer 7.x, Wasmer Edge
- **Wasm Tooling**: wasix 7.x (with volume support), wasm-pack, wasm-bindgen, wasm-tools 1.248.x

### Mobile & Native
- **Languages**: Kotlin (Android), Swift (iOS)
- **Build Tools**: Gradle, Trunk (Wasm bundler)

### Rust Toolchain & Quality Assurance
- **Manager**: rustup
- **Build/Dev**: cargo-leptos 0.3.6
- **Linting & Formatting**: cargo-fmt, cargo-clippy
- **Testing**: cargo test, cargo check

